        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-26T18:31:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This new host command of switching I2C bus ownership is new to me. I don\u0027t see it in the original proposal. Adding an extra software state complicates the design and I am not sure if all corner cases have been considered.\n\nActually, you can use `host_command_battery_get_static` instead of `host_command_battery_get_dynamic`. It by design uses the cached values.",
      "parentUuid": "9005da81_1236f3c5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "f299491c26ae4c52eb6d6a6456febec9503967d6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "32d624e6_3e4607be",
        "filename": "common/battery_v2.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 191,
      "author": {
        "id": 1532003
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-26T18:44:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This new host command of switching I2C bus ownership is new to me. I don\u0027t see it in the original proposal. Adding an extra software state complicates the design and I am not sure if all corner cases have been considered.\n\u003e \n\u003e Actually, you can use `host_command_battery_get_static` instead of `host_command_battery_get_dynamic`. It by design uses the cached values.\n\nYou\u0027re right about using static values as described in the design document, which aligns with the ADSP Lite solution. However, until the ADSP Lite solution is available (Q1\u002726), we need to use something meaningful to charge the battery and monitor its status. The dynamic solution is a temporary measure, and we\u0027ll only use the ADSP Lite-based solution once it\u0027s available (static/cached data will be in use in such scenario).",
      "parentUuid": "87a01e6b_72cc06e7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "f299491c26ae4c52eb6d6a6456febec9503967d6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ea1d5e78_434f35cb",
        "filename": "common/battery_v2.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 191,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-26T20:21:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From what you have described, there seems to be interactions of battery \u003c-\u003e EC \u003c-\u003e AP (mini-PD) and SMB charger \u003c-\u003e AP (mini-PD) at the same time, right? I\u0027d like to better understand the details of these interactions, like what battery information the mini-PD needs and how they are used. We may have other better approaches, like virtual battery, I2C tunneling, than using `host_command_battery_get_dynamic` and overloading it with extra features.",
      "parentUuid": "32d624e6_3e4607be",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "f299491c26ae4c52eb6d6a6456febec9503967d6",
